{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# World Models & Video Diffusion Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: 3D patchify for video"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class VideoPatch3D(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels=4, dim=64, patch_t=2, patch_h=2, patch_w=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.proj = nn.Conv3d("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            in_channels, dim,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            kernel_size=(patch_t, patch_h, patch_w),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            stride=(patch_t, patch_h, patch_w),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch_t = patch_t"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch_h = patch_h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch_w = patch_w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # x: (N, C, T, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.proj(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n, c, t, h, w = x.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens = x.reshape(n, c, t * h * w).transpose(1, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return tokens, (t, h, w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A 3D conv with stride equal to kernel acts as the spatio-temporal patchifier. `(T, H, W) -> (T/2, H/2, W/2)` grid of tokens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: 3D rotary position encoding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE) separately applied along `t`, `h`, `w` axes:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rope_3d(tokens, t_dim, h_dim, w_dim, grid):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens: (N, T*H*W, D)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid: (T, H, W) sizes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t_dim + h_dim + w_dim == D"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T, H, W = grid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n, seq, d = tokens.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if t_dim + h_dim + w_dim != d:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        raise ValueError(f\"t_dim+h_dim+w_dim ({t_dim}+{h_dim}+{w_dim}) must equal D={d}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    assert seq == T * H * W"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t_idx = torch.arange(T, device=tokens.device).repeat_interleave(H * W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h_idx = torch.arange(H, device=tokens.device).repeat_interleave(W).repeat(T)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w_idx = torch.arange(W, device=tokens.device).repeat(T * H)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # Simplified: just scale channels by frequencies. Real RoPE rotates pairs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs_t = torch.exp(-torch.log(torch.tensor(10000.0)) * torch.arange(t_dim // 2, device=tokens.device) / (t_dim // 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs_h = torch.exp(-torch.log(torch.tensor(10000.0)) * torch.arange(h_dim // 2, device=tokens.device) / (h_dim // 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs_w = torch.exp(-torch.log(torch.tensor(10000.0)) * torch.arange(w_dim // 2, device=tokens.device) / (w_dim // 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb_t = torch.cat([torch.sin(t_idx[:, None] * freqs_t), torch.cos(t_idx[:, None] * freqs_t)], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb_h = torch.cat([torch.sin(h_idx[:, None] * freqs_h), torch.cos(h_idx[:, None] * freqs_h)], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb_w = torch.cat([torch.sin(w_idx[:, None] * freqs_w), torch.cos(w_idx[:, None] * freqs_w)], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens + torch.cat([emb_t, emb_h, emb_w], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simplified additive form. Real RoPE rotates paired channels at frequencies; the positional information is the same."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Divided attention block"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DividedAttentionBlock(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, dim=64, heads=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.time_attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(dim, heads, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.space_attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(dim, heads, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln1 = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln2 = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln3 = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(dim, 4 * dim), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(4 * dim, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, grid):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        T, H, W = grid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n, seq, d = x.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # time attention: same (h, w), across t"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xt = x.view(n, T, H * W, d).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).reshape(n * H * W, T, d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a, _ = self.time_attn(self.ln1(xt), self.ln1(xt), self.ln1(xt), need_weights=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xt = (xt + a).reshape(n, H * W, T, d).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).reshape(n, seq, d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # space attention: same t, across (h, w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xs = xt.view(n, T, H * W, d).reshape(n * T, H * W, d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a, _ = self.space_attn(self.ln2(xs), self.ln2(xs), self.ln2(xs), need_weights=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xs = (xs + a).reshape(n, T, H * W, d).reshape(n, seq, d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        xs = xs + self.mlp(self.ln3(xs))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return xs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The time attention attends within each spatial position across time; the space attention attends within each frame across positions. Two O(T^2 + (HW)^2) operations instead of one O((THW)^2). This is the core of TimeSformer and every modern video DiT."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compose a tiny video DiT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyVideoDiT(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels=4, dim=64, depth=2, heads=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch = VideoPatch3D(in_channels=in_channels, dim=dim, patch_t=2, patch_h=2, patch_w=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList([DividedAttentionBlock(dim, heads) for _ in range(depth)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.out = nn.Linear(dim, in_channels * 2 * 2 * 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens, grid = self.patch(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for blk in self.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tokens = blk(tokens, grid)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.out(tokens), grid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Not a working video generator; a structural demo that every piece shapes correctly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Check shapes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vid = torch.randn(1, 4, 8, 16, 16)  # (N, C, T, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = TinyVideoDiT()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "out, grid = model(vid)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"input  {tuple(vid.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"tokens grid {grid}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output {tuple(out.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expect `grid = (4, 8, 8)` and `out = (1, 256, 32)` after patching; the head then projects to per-token spatio-temporal patches, ready to be un-patchified back into a video."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Compute the token count for a 5-second 360p video at patch-t=2, patch-h=8, patch-w=8. Reason about memory for attention at this size.\n2. **(Medium)** Swap the divided attention block above for a full joint attention block and measure the shape and parameter count. Explain why divided attention is necessary for real video models.\n3. **(Hard)** Build a minimal latent-action video model: take a dataset of (frame_t, action_t, frame_{t+1}) triples (any simple 2D game), train a tiny video DiT conditioned on action embeddings, and show that different actions produce different next frames."
      ]
    }
